      {
        "id": 4269,
        "name": "Mad Dog II: The Lost Gold",
        "summary": "The sequel to American Laser Game's original Mad Dog McCree, with pretty much the same gameplay and motion capture graphics. This PC conversion seems to have been tweaked a bit to be more stable than the original Mad Dog. There's also somewhat limited replay value as you can choose from 3 different guides for 3 different routes through the game.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1p5e.jpg",
        "release_date": 725760000,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Shooter|Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "52,9,5,6,50,13,78",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/mad-dog-ii-the-lost-gold",
        "cached_at": 1772529804
      },
      {
        "id": 4275,
        "name": "Flashback: The Quest for Identity",
        "summary": "Throughout the 20th century, an unprecedented political and economic crisis afflicted Earth, leading to the systematic disabling of it's programme to conquer outer space through lack of funding. The highest priority now was to carryout research into new energy sources, preservation of the enviro- ment and maintenance of the cultural heritage. However, at the dawn of the 21st century, provision of considerable funds from an unknown source released by the politicians of the new, unified government, permitted a return to the space research programme.\n\nThe conquest began gradually with the construction of huge, manned artificial satellites. Several lunar bases were created with the view to becoming future Earth colonies within the solar system. The considerable advancements made together with the supply of increasingly greater sums of money allowed man to explore, even as far as the planet Titan.\n\nYou play the part of Conrad Hart, controlling his every move through the 6 levels of the game. During your quest, you will come across many different friends and foes whom you may wish to help or vanquish using your gun. you will have to complete many challenges in order to restore your lost memory. Each level features its own unique graphics and hazards, linked by cinematic animation sequences.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co6fda.jpg",
        "release_date": 723168000,
        "rating": 82.98576823149597,
        "rating_count": 108,
        "genres": "Platform|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "116,117,19,29,50,14,13,16,62,78",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/flashback-the-quest-for-identity",
        "cached_at": 1772529804
      },
      {
        "id": 4281,
        "name": "Who Shot Johnny Rock?",
        "summary": "Another live-actor arcade shooter by American Laser Games (makers of Mad Dog McCree and Crime Patrol), Who Shot Johnny Rock is set in the classic 1920's style gangster era.\n\nAs the title suggests, you're supposed to find out who shot singer Johnny Rock (or at least who hired the guys who shot him) and put them behind bars.\n\nThere are some differences between this game and previous American Laser Games shooters. Instead of a wimpy pistol, you get a tommy gun (which doesn't need to be reloaded). Unfortunately, you also have limited ammo and need to buy more at times. Instead of lives you have a fixed supply of money, and each time you die you lose some cash. Lose it all and it's game over.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1p6h.jpg",
        "release_date": 694137600,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Shooter|Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "52,117,50,13,78",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/who-shot-johnny-rock",
        "cached_at": 1772529804
      },
      {
        "id": 4283,
        "name": "MegaRace",
        "summary": "Virtual Television has given us a chance to do the things that we can't make real in everyday life: Race through 14 great tracks in 5 different environments in a totally virtual place where you can kill each other quite easily with sidekicks or guns. In every track you will see some symbols that can make your car speed up, slow up or even blow up, like your mega-host Lance Boyle says, \"Who knows; who cares!\" Everything you see in MegaRace is virtual and no one really dies there. So have fun!",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co3z1i.jpg",
        "release_date": 757296000,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Racing",
        "platform_ids": "3,6,50,14,13,78",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/megarace",
        "cached_at": 1772529804
      },
      {
        "id": 4291,
        "name": "Supreme Warrior",
        "summary": "Supreme Warrior is a full-motion video fighting game. The game, or interactive movie, is set in China hundreds of years ago. You are tasked with protecting half of a magical mask. The wearer of the mask will be granted untold power. Unfortunately, the villanous Wang Tu has the other half of the mask, and wants your half badly. So, you must fight off Wang Tu's minions, and eventually Fang Tu himself.\n\nThe gameplay in Supreme Warrior consists of digitized video with interactive elements. At many points during the video, you can unleash a punch, kick, or block. If your timing is correct, you inflict damage on your opponent. If you timing is off, your opponent hurts you.",
